{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JApRMPjcowXgJ66ZjXobPU","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## 2026-08-30 — WI-535: adjudicator telemetry first, dial off\n2\t\n3\tStep 1 of the adjudicator session-retention plan's sequenced work\n4\t(`docs/plans/2026-08-29-adjudicator-session-retention-plan.md#5-sequenced-work-each-a-wi-none-starts-while--exists`).\n5\tOI-69 (step 2, the owner rulings) is already ruled, and its recommendation\n6\tnames this telemetry row as unblocked with the dial off; WI-540 (the\n7\tretention layer proper) needs it.\n8\t\n9\tDeferred open items: none — telemetry-only row, no owner decision owed.\n10\t\n11\t### What landed\n12\t\n13\t- `docs/agents.toml` — `OPENCODE-GROK`'s `version` cell and `notes` prose\n14\t  still read \"4.5\" after a prior session (`9ab30d64`) corrected the `model`\n15\t  cell and the family comment to `grok-4.6`; the remaining two cells now\n16\t  match.\n17\t- `project-trajectory/scripts/agent_loop.py` — new\n18\t  `family_context_telemetry(family, data)`: per family, the session id and\n19\t  context occupancy/window/percent read straight off the process's own JSON\n20\t  result, no mint/resume/adapter. ANTHROPIC's stream-json result already\n21\t  carries `session_id`, and occupancy/window come from the same `usage` /\n22\t  `modelUsage` fields `session_meta` already partially reads (occupancy =\n23\t  input + cache-read + cache-creation + output; window = the `modelUsage`\n24\t  entry whose own input/output counts match those same totals, so a\n25\t  subagent's aside on a different model is never mistaken for the session's\n26\t  own window — left blank on no exact match rather than guessed, per the\n27\t  plan's own \"never guessed\" rule). OPENAI/OPENCODE return blank today: their\n28\t  shipped one-shot templates carry no `--json`/`--format json`, so there is\n29\t  nothing to parse until WI-540's adapter lands.\n30\t- `session_meta` now writes four more columns: `session-id`,\n31\t  `context-used`, `context-window`, `context-pct`.\n32\t- `project-trajectory/scripts/agent_common.py` — `write_session_log`'s\n33\t  header-key tuple carries the same four keys; `regenerate_index` gained a\n34\t  `Ctx %` column in the generated `docs/iteration_index.md` table (not\n35\t  touched directly — the trunk lane regenerates it).\n36\t- Tests: extended\n37\t  `tests/test_agent_loop_policy.py::test_session_meta_is_the_log_row_in_the_logs_own_column_order`\n38\t  for the four new keys; added coverage for `family_context_telemetry`\n39\t  (ANTHROPIC exact-match window pick, ANTHROPIC with no usage at all, and the\n40\t  non-ANTHROPIC blank path) and for `write_session_log` carrying the new\n41\t  header keys through.\n42\t\n43\t### Harness\n44\t\n45\t_(filled at close)_\n46\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65bdbdd4-2f55-47db-b6b2-f63ae7bf32bb","uuid":"3ee61212-81da-496f-9014-020c493a6bc4","timestamp":"2026-08-31T01:24:15.042Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-drive\\wi-535-adjudicator-telemetry-first\\docs\\log.d\\WI-535-adjudicator-telemetry-first.md","content":"## 2026-08-30 — WI-535: adjudicator telemetry first, dial off\n\nStep 1 of the adjudicator session-retention plan's sequenced work\n(`docs/plans/2026-08-29-adjudicator-session-retention-plan.md#5-sequenced-work-each-a-wi-none-starts-while--exists`).\nOI-69 (step 2, the owner rulings) is already ruled, and its recommendation\nnames this telemetry row as unblocked with the dial off; WI-540 (the\nretention layer proper) needs it.\n\nDeferred open items: none — telemetry-only row, no owner decision owed.\n\n### What landed\n\n- `docs/agents.toml` — `OPENCODE-GROK`'s `version` cell and `notes` prose\n  still read \"4.5\" after a prior session (`9ab30d64`) corrected the `model`\n  cell and the family comment to `grok-4.6`; the remaining two cells now\n  match.\n- `project-trajectory/scripts/agent_loop.py` — new\n  `family_context_telemetry(family, data)`: per family, the session id and\n  context occupancy/window/percent read straight off the process's own JSON\n  result, no mint/resume/adapter. ANTHROPIC's stream-json result already\n  carries `session_id`, and occupancy/window come from the same `usage` /\n  `modelUsage` fields `session_meta` already partially reads (occupancy =\n  input + cache-read + cache-creation + output; window = the `modelUsage`\n  entry whose own input/output counts match those same totals, so a\n  subagent's aside on a different model is never mistaken for the session's\n  own window — left blank on no exact match rather than guessed, per the\n  plan's own \"never guessed\" rule). OPENAI/OPENCODE return blank today: their\n  shipped one-shot templates carry no `--json`/`--format json`, so there is\n  nothing to parse until WI-540's adapter lands.\n- `session_meta` now writes four more columns: `session-id`,\n  `context-used`, `context-window`, `context-pct`.\n- `project-trajectory/scripts/agent_common.py` — `write_session_log`'s\n  header-key tuple carries the same four keys; `regenerate_index` gained a\n  `Ctx %` column in the generated `docs/iteration_index.md` table (not\n  touched directly — the trunk lane regenerates it).\n- Tests: extended\n  `tests/test_agent_loop_policy.py::test_session_meta_is_the_log_row_in_the_logs_own_column_order`\n  for the four new keys; added coverage for `family_context_telemetry`\n  (ANTHROPIC exact-match window pick, ANTHROPIC with no usage at all, and the\n  non-ANTHROPIC blank path) and for `write_session_log` carrying the new\n  header keys through.\n\n### Harness\n\n_(filled at close)_\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}}}
